    "created_at": "2026-04-21T15:56:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-21T15:56:36Z",
    "body": "T? as dictionary member is only tri-state with a default value. Otherwise you have a quad-state. Which I think we have at least one legitimate example of, but prolly also many illegitimate.\n\nAnd then coupled with that we want to discourage null in favor of undefined. And we prolly don’t want to rewrite everything.\n\nMaybe TriState and QuadState is the most straightforward for now?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
